// 09 · all eight, at once — one program the medium reads eight ways
//
// The eight files before this each took one aspect. This one is a whole small
// program, and all eight are present in it together. Run it: it prints 53 — a
// Pure seed of 50, raised three times through an effect the handler counts
// (0, then 1, then 2, so +3), borrowed by reference, and printed. Small, but
// every tentacle has something true to read.
//
// Then open it in the medium and walk the ring across the addresses at the
// bottom. At each, the named facet reads from the compiler's own graph — the
// same eight-aspect projection `mentl edit` shows, at a one-shot address.
//
// Run it:   mentl run  lib/tutorial/09-all.mn
// Edit it:  mentl space   →   http://localhost:7378/ide/
import io

// #6 refinement — Level is an Int proven to sit in 0..100 wherever one is built.
type Level = Int where 0 <= self && self <= 100

// #2 handlers + #1 the graph — the Bump effect and the handler that counts it.
// Every binding here is a live handle the graph chases; there is no symbol
// table beside it.
effect Bump {
  bump() -> Int
}

handler counter with n = 0 {
  bump() => resume(n) with n = n + 1,
}

// #4 the row + #7 the gradient — `with Pure` states, and the medium proves,
// that this body performs nothing; the annotation is the input that unlocks it.
fn seed() -> Level with Pure = 50

// #5 ownership — `ref` borrows the value; reading it never consumes it.
fn keep(ref x) = x

// #3 the verbs — raise threads the counted bumps into the base and carries the
// Bump row; run composes seed into raise into keep with |>; main installs the
// handler with ~> and pipes the result out with |>, too.
fn raise(base) with Bump = base + bump() + bump() + bump()

fn run() with Bump = seed() |> raise |> keep

fn main() = {
  let total = run() ~> counter
  total |> int_to_str |> print_string
}

// #8 the Reason — every type and row above carries a Reason edge, and the Why
// walk reads it back to the literal or the unification that set it.
//
// Walk the ring. `mentl <address>` projects the aspects at a position, and one
// read shows several at once — that is the whole point: the graph read many
// ways from one place.
//
//   mentl lib/tutorial/09-all.mn:40:20   — raise, mid-body: five facets at once.
//        Query is the type; row is `Effects: Bump`; ownership is `own`; the
//        gradient offers a step; and Why walks the Reason chain.
//   mentl lib/tutorial/09-all.mn:35:9    — keep's parameter: ownership reads `ref`.
//   mentl lib/tutorial/09-all.mn:32:4    — seed: the type carries the Level
//        refinement (`() -> Level`) and the row reads `Pure`.
//
// Two aspects live elsewhere, honestly. The verb facet reads the shape you
// wrote — the topology is on the page, so the ring reads it there. And the
// propose facet fills only at a hole: replace a bump() in raise with `??` and
// the socket surfaces a proven survivor, but a `??` makes the program
// non-executable, so this running file leaves it out. The eighth aspect is the
// one that lives in an unfinished program.

